"The Salt Halls are the drowned halls of a dead sea people, a slice of another world set in the rock."
"Its walls glitter with salt crust and give a faint green glow, enough to see by close up."
"Its halls are knee-deep in cold seawater in places, and dry on the stairs and landings."
"Silt-wights haunt the halls: the drowned dead of the sea people, slow, grey and grasping."
"A silt-wight is level 3, with a crushing grip; it is slow on stairs and dry ground."
"Salt burns silt-wights, and a fistful of the crust flung in one's face makes it recoil."
"The dungeon's boss is the Tidewarden, a huge crab in barnacled bronze, level 7."
"The Tidewarden guards the lowest hall, where a silver chest sits on a drowned altar."
"The silver chest holds a sealskin pack that keeps what is put in it dry, and 40 knowledge points."
"Clearing the Salt Halls gives a quest reward and experience enough for several levels."
"Time in a dungeon runs as outside; the sea cave floods at high tide and traps those within."
"The halls' upper landing is safe from cinderstorms and from every beast of the isle."
"The dungeon holds the notice: Recommended level: 5."
